          "question": "e-4431",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Given two ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/assets/c17e75a26e1dbfa0e89535380e33c9a232a5db7bb2841dec7a03b0fbe861b8c4.png) matrices ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/assets/0dffbd47bb64c877dbb545c2c5024e2e50ce9ec516b7a4509d53f77916e8c791.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/assets/c40e3405d51242d87b13698d1e715c1b391185890487e3d2a386cb09d3b952e9.png) we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/assets/aae29aab049034fe50debd00d825e5e37b19de8f1a803dfb098727bbf8afe0e9.png)\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/assets/bf7493e53cfed1ef296dcc0f7020d7ceec014af63a0cbee3f8cac5e1a11afd0d.png)\n\nWe can compute the required determinants as follows:\n\n- For the first determinant, we notice that it's upper triangular. Therefore, the determinant is simply the product of the diagonal entries.\n\n- For the second determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion down the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/assets/c23fa2f99aef303059a834682e511943ffbe022294cf2d9ac8e72e707316a607.png)st column.\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/assets/b968eb1cf6b8a72d8f4b46202ea1a6ab201145ae2531bfe2b5a2049aafae9b28.png)",
