    {
      "question": "e-4432",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "09c014a5fdf460d0ee3988faa68f02d9ecdb1b6b6b8a20fb040d53af310449a2",
      "new_sha256": "3a2e9c3eca4ea8566e68d5d012c879d0d8600b6f2b0fc57393f25000f19c72c9",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-4432",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n|A^{-1}| = \\dfrac{1}{|A|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $|A|$ using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 14 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-12+7) \\\\  & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\det(A^{-1}) =  \\dfrac{1}{|A|} = -\\dfrac{1}{15}.\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/example-4432.json",
          "file_sha256": "591aa94f04fc2563cf1cd6e5bd203ade6ae501d2de0c66188cdfbcd3df3781b0"
        }
